    "note": "Reviewed every build, runtime, optional/development and Node direct candidate, including current upper bounds. Hypothesis 6.168.3 is the sole newer candidate since the reviewed 0.44.0 receipt. Official release notes (https://github.com/HypothesisWorks/hypothesis/releases/tag/v6.168.3 and https://hypothesis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/changelog.html) describe removal of quadratic pytest-statistics summarization for very large example counts. Installed 6.168.3 in the local development environment and passed 61 schema artifact codec tests plus 3 schema property tests with pytest -n 0. All other registry candidates and dependency constraints are unchanged; every candidate remains within declared bounds and supports Python 3.14. No dependency manifest changes or runtime dependency upgrades are needed. This release changes diagnostic log protocol to schema 2 and bounded file-decision reads; database schema 9 is unchanged. The exact-tree bounded release gate is separate evidence.",
